.Dd May 31, 2026
.Dt SWIFTLY-CLEAN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm swiftly-clean
.Nd deep-clean Xcode and Swift Package Manager build state
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -force
.Op Fl -deep
.Op Fl -dry-run
.Nm
.Fl -resolve
.Op Fl -force
.Op Fl -dry-run
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Nm
.Fl -help
.Nm
.Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
removes common Xcode and Swift Package Manager build state from the current
user account and, when present, the local
.Pa .build
directory in the current working directory.
.Pp
By default,
.Nm
removes Xcode DerivedData, the global SwiftPM cache, SwiftPM security
fingerprints, and the local
.Pa .build
directory when it exists.
.Pp
With
.Fl -deep ,
.Nm
removes the full SwiftPM user state instead of only SwiftPM security
fingerprints.
.Pp
With
.Fl -resolve ,
.Nm
searches the current directory tree for
.Pa Package.resolved
files and offers to delete them.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -force
Skip confirmation prompts.
.It Fl -deep
Remove full SwiftPM user state instead of only security fingerprints.
.It Fl -dry-run
Show what would be removed without deleting anything.
.It Fl -resolve
Find
.Pa Package.resolved
files and offer to delete them.
.It Fl -version
Print the installed command's version.
.It Fl -help , Fl h
Show help.
.El
.Sh SAFETY
.Nm
prompts before deleting files unless
.Fl -force
is used.
.Pp
.Fl -dry-run
prints the cleanup targets and exits without deleting anything, before
confirmation prompts, Xcode checks, or delete calls.
.Pp
Deletion is guarded so cleanup targets must be expected paths under
.Pa ~/Library
or the local
.Pa .build
directory, and package resolution cleanup is guarded so only files named
.Pa Package.resolved
under the current working directory are eligible for deletion.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData
Xcode DerivedData.
.It Pa ~/Library/Caches/org.swift.swiftpm
SwiftPM global cache.
.It Pa ~/Library/org.swift.swiftpm/security
SwiftPM security fingerprints.
.It Pa ~/Library/org.swift.swiftpm
Full SwiftPM user state used by
.Fl -deep .
.It Pa ./.build
Local SwiftPM build directory in the current working directory.
.It Pa Package.resolved
SwiftPM resolved package file searched by
.Fl -resolve .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
.Nm
exits 0 when help, version, dry-run, skipped cleanup, or successful cleanup
completes normally, and exits non-zero for unknown options or safety guard
failures.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Show what the default cleanup would remove:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
swiftly-clean --dry-run
.Ed
.Pp
Show what a deep cleanup would remove:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
swiftly-clean --deep --dry-run
.Ed
.Pp
Run the default cleanup interactively:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
swiftly-clean
.Ed
.Pp
Run a deep cleanup without confirmation prompts:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
swiftly-clean --force --deep
.Ed
.Pp
Search for
.Pa Package.resolved
files and choose which ones to delete:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
swiftly-clean --resolve
.Ed
.Pp
Print the installed command's version:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
swiftly-clean --version
.Ed
.Pp
Show command help:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
swiftly-clean --help
.Ed
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Jamie Brannan
